00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.405
&gt;&gt;&gt; TO AVOID ARMAGEDDON NASA
ANNOUNCING THE SPACECRAFT PUSHED

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:10.443
AN ASTEROID OUT OF ORBIT AFTER A
DELIBERATE CRASH LAST MONTH.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:15.381
THE GOAL WAS TO SEE IF SLAMMING
INTO THE ASTEROID COULD CHANGE

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:19.419
ITS COURSE JUST IN CASE A BIGGER
ASTEROID ONE DAY THREATENS

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:22.755
EARTH.
&gt;&gt; NOW THIS IS A WATERSHED

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:26.025
MOMENT FOR PLANETARY DEFENSE.
AND A WATERSHED MOMENT FOR

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:32.598
HUMANITY.
&gt;&gt; LET'S BRING IN CNN SPACE AND

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:34.267
DEFENSE CORRESPONDENT KRISTEN
FISHER.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.036
IT TOOK A WHILE TO FIGURE OUT
EXACTLY WHAT HAPPENED HERE.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:39.906
IS IT WORTH IT?
IS THE PAYOFF THERE?

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:43.209
&gt;&gt; Reporter: YOU AND I HAVE BEEN
TALKING ABOUT THIS FOR WEEKS.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:46.679
WHAT WE LEARNED YESTERDAY WAS
THIS MISSION WAS MORE SUCCESSFUL

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:51.117
THAN NASA EXPECTED.
WE KNEW THE DART SPACECRAFT HAD

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:55.188
SUCCESSFULLY HIT THIS ASTEROID A
LITTLE OVER TWO WEEKS AGO.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:01:01.528
WHAT WE DID NOT KNOW IS IF NASA
ACHIEVED THE PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:06.699
WHICH WAS TO MOVE ITS ORBIT JUST
A LITTLE BIT.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:15.642
IT ORBITS THIS LARGER ASTEROID O
THE GOAL WAS TO PUSH IT CLOSER

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:19.179
TO THIS ASTEROID TO SEE IF THEY
COULD DO IT.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:23.950
WHAT THEY FOUND WAS SHOCKING.
BECAUSE THEY WERE EXPECTING TO

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:27.854
CHANGE THE ORBIT BY ONLY ABOUT
10 MINUTES.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:31.691
IN REALITY THEY WERE ABLE TO
CHANGE IT BY 32 MINUTES.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:37.530
BEFORE IMPACT THE ORBIT WAS 11
HOURS AND 55 IMPACTS, AFTER

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.567
IMPACT, 11 HOURS AND 23 MINUTES
AROUND.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:44.070
THAT'S A CHANGE OF ABOUT 4%.
THE WAY THEY WERE ABLE TO

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:48.241
DETERMINE ALL OF THIS IS USING
GROUND BASED TELESCOPES.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:53.112
TELESCOPES YOU AND I ARE USED TO
ON THE GROUND, ON PLANET EARTH,

00:01:53.112 --> 00:02:00.253
LIKE THIS ONE IN CHILE, THAT'S
WHY IT TOOK TIME FOR YOU AND I

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:02.689
TO LEARN WHAT WE'VE BEEN WAITING
FOR ALL THIS TIME.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:05.725
&gt;&gt; THAT LOOKS LIKE THE MORE YOU
KNOW LOGO, THE PICTURE, I

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:09.696
THOUGHT THAT THE WHOLE TIME.
THE GOAL OF THE MISSION WAS TO

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:15.001
SEE IF IT WAS FEASIBLE TO MOVE A
POTENTIAL EARTH-THREATENING

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:23.977
ASTEROID IN THE FUTURE WITHOUT
TRAINING A RAG TAG GROUP OF OIL

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:30.183
DRILLERS INCLUDING BEN AFFLECK
AND BRUCE WILLIS, BECAUSE THEY

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:36.322
MAY NOT BE AVAILABLE.
&gt;&gt; YEAH, WE LEARNED HUMANITY MAY

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:40.093
NOT NEED BRUCE WILLIS AND BEN
AFFLECK.

